# SK packages of the fleet runtime: exact pins, REQUIRED on every chi host.
#
# Input to the lock, not the lock itself. deploy/fleet-constraints.txt is the
# fully resolved lock generated from this file, deploy/fleet-tools.in and
# deploy/fleet-self.in (skcapstone's own '.[fleet-qualify]'): run
# scripts/fleet-lock.sh after any change here and commit both files in the same
# PR (Renovate does this itself for its own PRs). CI
# (.github/workflows/fleet-lock.yml) refuses a lock that is stale, does not
# install, fails `pip check`, lowers a security package, carries a known
# vulnerability, or depends on an upper cap missing from deploy/dependency-caps.md.
#
# Every pin here must be installed on a host after rollout, or the parity gate
# halts with DEPENDENCY_DRIFT (src/skcapstone/fleet/dependency_parity.py).
#
# skskills: 1.2.1 is the first release without the rich<14 cap.
# skbrain: 1.0.2 is the first release without the click<8.2 / typer<0.13 caps,
#   which pulled the fleet down to click 8.1.8 and typer 0.12.5 (#1382).
#
# Rules: exact `==` pins only. A pyproject floor must never exceed its pin
# (tests/test_fleet_dependency_parity.py). To bump, see
# docs/fleet/DEPLOY-FROM-MAIN.md "Bumping a fleet dependency".
